course: dictionary
lesson: 2503
title: Finding and fixing bugs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A program follows its steps exactly, so one wrong step can make the whole thing go wrong. «A robot follows its steps exactly; a mistake in the steps is called a bug, and finding and fixing it is called debugging.»
explain: Debugging works step by step. Run the program, see what goes wrong, find the line with the mistake, then fix it. «Debug the code» means doing exactly that.
explain: «Rubber duck debugging means explaining your code line by line to a toy or a friend; saying it out loud often helps you spot the mistake.» Next time you are stuck, try explaining your code out loud to someone.
fact: A bug is a mistake in a program.
fact: Debugging means finding and fixing bugs.
fact: «Every bug has a cause», so there is always a reason something went wrong.
fact: «Debug your program» means find and fix its mistakes.
fact: Debugging can also mean finding and fixing problems in any plan or machine.
exercise: What is a bug in a program? | A toy duck that quacks | A kind of computer screen | A fast way to run code | *A mistake in the program
exercise: What does debugging mean? | Turning the computer off | *Finding and fixing mistakes | Writing a brand new program from scratch | Painting the code in bright colours
exercise: «Every bug has a cause.» What does this tell you? | Bugs happen by magic and cannot be found | Bugs never need fixing | *There is always a reason something went wrong | Only robots make bugs
test: In the sentence «debug the code», what does debug mean? | To copy the code into a new file | To delete the whole program | *To find and fix the mistakes in the code | To run the program
test: Why might Maya explain her code out loud to a rubber duck? | *Saying it out loud often helps her spot the mistake | The duck will fix the bug for her | Ducks are the fastest computers | Rubber ducks make programs run faster
exam: Which step comes first when you debug a program? | Turn the computer off | Fix the line | *Run the program | Find the line with the mistake
